<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n51750" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καθέρπω</span></b> , aor. 1
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καθείρπῠσα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Ra.</u>
					485
				</span></i>
			:—<i>creep, steal down</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπ᾽ ὀρθίων πάγων καθεῖρπεν ἔλαφος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					89
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καθέρπυσόν νυν ἐς Κεραμεικόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Ra.</u>
					129
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				485
			</span></i>: metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρὰ τὰ ὦτα ἄρτι ἴουλος καθέρπει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Smp.</u>
					4.23
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>return</i> from exile, <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				306.54
			</span></i> (Delph., from Tegea, <span class="entity">iv B.C.</span>): in this signf.
			the aor.
			part. is <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατενθών</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				4
			</span></i>; pf.
			part.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατηνθηκώς</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				39
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
